  "scoring_key_verified": true,
  "notes": "Original Robinson et al. (2001) short-form key as stated in the Portuguese confirmatory study (source_url): authoritative 15 items = warmth & involvement {1, 7, 12, 14, 27} + reasoning/induction {5, 11, 25, 29, 31} + democratic participation {3, 9, 18, 21, 22}; authoritarian 12 items = corporal punishment {2, 6, 19, 32} + verbal hostility {13, 16, 23, 30} + punitive strategies {4, 10, 26, 28}; permissive 5 items = lack of follow-through {8, 15, 17, 20, 24}. This corrects the previously assumed key (item 4 was listed as permissive and item 17 as authoritarian). Styles are means on the 1–5 scale (1 = never … 5 = always); no reverse-keyed items. Confirm item numbering against the official form when transcribing text. Between-parent gap per style is computed in instruments/couple.ts.",
  "source_url": "https://www.redalyc.org/journal/1293/129355455001/html/",
  "text_source": "Item text not populated (obtain the 32-item short form from Robinson et al. 2001 or the authors). Scoring key verified 2026-09-16 from the open-access confirmatory factor analysis of the PSDQ short form in a Portuguese sample (Redalyc), which states the original Robinson et al. (2001) item assignment."
